From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment <experiment@invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: treat an active data phase as pending receive work

This driver has no receive interrupt: every receive record, including the TCP
ACKs that keep a sender's window open, is drained inside the join worker. The
pump predicate therefore left the worker on the 20 ms idle interval whenever
the TX queue momentarily emptied, so inbound records waited up to one idle
interval.

Count an active data phase as pending work so the short interval applies while
connected. Scheduling only: no change to depth, credit accounting, PID
ownership, deadlines or join admission, and the existing bounded no-progress
guard still prevents an unbounded spin.

Measurement profile only; not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c	2026-10-23 13:27:09
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/mac.c	2026-10-23 13:27:09
@@ -4247,9 +4247,16 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_MT6797_CCMP_TX_PUMP
 	if (ccmp_stable_epoch && !mt6797_snapshot_active(mac->snapshot)) {
 		unsigned int delay_ms;
+		/* A connected data phase can deliver a record (including a TCP ACK
+		 * for a frame just sent) at any moment, and this driver has no RX
+		 * interrupt: every receive runs inside this worker. Treat an active
+		 * data phase as pending work so the short interval applies, not the
+		 * idle one. Bounded by the existing no-progress guard.
+		 */
 		bool pending = !skb_queue_empty(&mac->join_queue) ||
 			mac->join_inflight || mac->data_slots.count || mac->join_credit_pending ||
-			mac->join_page_debt || mac->join_data_page_debt;
+			mac->join_page_debt || mac->join_data_page_debt ||
+			(mac->join_data_phase && !mac->join_data_ended);
 
 		delay_ms = mt6797_join_pump_delay(&mac->join_pump_zero_runs,
 						  pending, pump_progress);
